he Series A Preferred Stock, Series C Preferred Stock, Series D Preferred Stock, Series E Preferred Stock, Series F Preferred Stock, Series G Preferred Stock, and Series H Preferred Stock, voting together as a separate series, shall be entitled to elect one ( 1) director of the Corporation (the "Series H Director", together with the Series B Director and any Additional Preferred Directors, the "Preferred Directors"). The Series H Director may be removed without cause by, and only by, the affirmative vote of the holders of a majority of the Series A Preferred Stock, Series C Preferred Stock, Series D Preferred Stock, Series E Preferred Stock, Series F Preferred Stock, Series G Preferred Stock, and Series H Preferred Stock, voting together as a separate series, given either at a special meeting of such stockholders duly called for that purpose or pursuant to a written consent of such stockholders. The holders of Common Stock and Charter Preferred Stock, voting together as a separate class, shall be entitled to elect one (1) director of the Corporation (the "Common Director"). The Common Director may be removed without cause by, and only by, the affirmative vote of the holders of a majority of the Common Stock and Charter Preferred Stock, voting together as a separate class, given either at a special meeting of such stockholders duly called for that purpose or pursuant to a written consent of such stockholders. The holders of Series A Preferred Stock, Series B Preferred Stock, Series C Preferred Stock, Series D Preferred Stock, Series E Preferred Stock, Series F Preferred Stock, Series G Preferred Stock, and Series H Preferred Stock voting as a single class and on an as-converted basis, shall be entitled to elect the Additional Preferred Directors in accordance with Subsection 6(a). Any Additional Preferred Director so elected may be removed without cause by, and only by, the affirmative vote of the holders of at least sixty-five percent (65%) of the outstanding shares